                <pb facs="1138" n="1022" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 718.1915/224.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Cresson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram November 25. I have received from the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs assurances no change in status quo has occurred or is contemplated on
                    Costa Rican boundary. New officials instructed to this effect were lately on
                    Pacific side but no newly created offices.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cresson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
